14:37.380 --> 14:38.160
You would think so,

14:38.240 --> 14:40.520
but here is where the math performs a magic trick.

14:40.980 --> 14:43.080
The leaky protocol only leaks

14:43.080 --> 14:46.220
if that specific parallel run outputs a 1 condition.

14:47.040 --> 14:48.400
The mathematics of the encoding

14:48.400 --> 14:51.000
ensure that out of those 100 parallel runs,

14:51.200 --> 14:53.500
the probability is overwhelmingly high

14:53.500 --> 14:54.940
that at least one of those runs

14:54.940 --> 14:56.660
will hit a zero output condition.

14:56.840 --> 14:57.180
And remember,

14:57.320 --> 14:59.440
the zero output condition leaks absolutely nothing.

14:59.660 --> 14:59.920
I see.

15:00.180 --> 15:01.880
So the math proves that with a probability

15:01.880 --> 15:04.360
of 1 minus 2 to the negative tau plus 1,

15:04.660 --> 15:06.160
at least one of your secret shares

15:06.160 --> 15:07.320
will pass through the system

15:07.320 --> 15:09.240
completely cloaked in a zero state.

15:09.460 --> 15:10.640
Wait, let me make sure I'm getting this.

15:10.680 --> 15:13.260
So even if 99 out of the 100 runs

15:13.260 --> 15:14.120
leaks some data

15:14.120 --> 15:16.140
because it's a secret sharing scheme,

15:16.500 --> 15:18.460
the attacker needs all 100 pieces

15:18.460 --> 15:20.160
to rebuild my original input.

